# Build context for docker/server/Dockerfile and docker/broker/Dockerfile
# (both built with `-f docker/<tier>/Dockerfile .` from the repo root —
# see either file's own header). Keeping this list correct matters for
# more than build speed: `.env`/`.env.*` below is what stops a real
# secret from ever landing in an image layer.

.git
.github

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local, developer- or install-produced state — never baked into an
# image; the real equivalents are volumes at container runtime
# (docker/compose.yaml).
data
backups
e2e/.auth
e2e/dist
test-results
playwright-report
graphify-out

# Secrets. `.env.example` (no real values, tracked in git) is the only
# env file that should ever reach a build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

installer/*.log
*.log

.DS_Store
